  "plan": {
    "goal": "Culture a human proximal-tubule channel reproducing the in vivo apical fluid shear of 0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa).",
    "rationale": "The canonical in vivo proximal-tubule apical shear of 0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa) is the physiological target. A 400 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm PDMS channel at 0.8 µL/min (water-like medium, 1e-3 Pa·s) delivers exactly 0.02 Pa wall shear (confirmed by forward wall_shear_stress), with Re ≈ 0.05 (firmly laminar) and a 60 s residence time. Proximal-tubule cells are seeded at 100,000 cells/cm² (standard renal epithelial density) → 8,000 cells in the 0.08 cm² channel. Note: proximal tubule is not in the physiology registry, so the 0.2 dyn/cm² target is taken as the user-supplied canonical published value and should be verified against the specific literature for the chosen cell source.",
